~ statements are wrapped in parentheses — they read as asides, never as instructions.
~ conditionals reference already-defined static data only.

#book: { status - draft }

(if @book.status is draft)
@aside Draft — do not distribute. aside@
(end)

~ with else

~ note: a record value cannot contain a literal @ (it starts a node), so
~ store the local-part and host separately rather than a whole address.

#author: { corresponding - true, name - Aldous Vane, affiliation - Dunmore Head Station }

(if @author.corresponding is true)
Corresponding author: @author.name, @author.affiliation.
(else)
@author.name
(end)

~ conditionals nest freely

#report: { status - final, audience - external }

(if @report.status is final)
(if @report.audience equals external)
@aside Reviewed and approved for external circulation. aside@
(else)
@aside Final — internal only. aside@
(end)
(end)

~ (if) inside (each) filters rows: only operational stations reach the
~ table. combine with @row/@col to build a filtered table from a collection.

#network: [
  { name - Dunmore Head, status - operational }
  { name - Carrick Point, status - closed }
  { name - Ines Rock, status - operational }
]

@table |caption Operational stations|
  @row @col Site col@ @col Status col@ row@
  (each @network as s)
  (if @s.status is operational)
  @row @col @s.name col@ @col @s.status col@ row@
  (end)
  (end)
table@
